/* book Worked example: Q: A square plate 800 mm × 800 mm × 4 mm is simply supported on all edges, with E = 70 GPa and ν = 0.30, and carries a lateral pressure of 1 kPa. (a) Find D, the centre deflection and the centre bending moment and stress. (b) A compression Nx = 10 kN/m is added on two opposite edges. Find Nx/Ncr, the single-term magnified deflection and the exact series value. (c) What would a tension of 10 kN/m do instead?
   1. Units: a = b = 0.8 m, t = 0.004 m, q = 1000 N/m², E = 70 × 10⁹ N/m².
   2. D = 70 × 10⁹ × (0.004)³/[12 × 0.91] = 4480/10.92 = 410.3 N·m.
   3. Centre deflection: q a⁴/D = 1000 × 0.8⁴/410.3 = 409.6/410.3 = 0.9984 m, so wmax = 0.00406 × 0.9984 = 4.05 mm. Summing the Navier series directly gives 4.06 mm (coefficient 0.00406).
   4. Centre moment: Mx = 0.0479 q a² = 0.0479 × 1000 × 0.64 = 30.7 N·m/m (series 30.6). Face stress σ = 6Mx/t² = 6 × 30.6/(1.6 × 10⁻⁵) = 11.5 MPa.
   5. Buckling load of the square plate (m = n = 1): Ncr = 4π²D/b² = 4 × 9.870 × 410.3/0.64 = 25,307 N/m = 25.3 kN/m. Nx/Ncr = 10/25.3 = 0.395.
   6. Single-term magnification: 1/(1 − 0.395) = 1.653, so w ≈ 1.653 × 4.06 = 6.71 mm.
   7. Exact series with each term divided by its own (1 − N/Nmn): w = 6.76 mm, a factor 1.667. The higher terms have much larger Nmn, so they are hardly magnified; the single-term estimate is within 0.8%.
   8. Tension of 10 kN/m: the first term is divided by 1 + 0.395 instead, and the series gives w = 2.89 mm, 29% less than with no in-plane force.
   Answer: D = 410.3 N·m; wmax = 4.06 mm, Mx = 30.6 N·m/m, σ = 11.5 MPa. With 10 kN/m compression Nx/Ncr = 0.395 and w ≈ 6.7 mm (6.76 mm exactly); with 10 kN/m tension w = 2.89 mm. */
